7218,'How about not showing the default signature if it&#39;s not edited :) Some sorta toggle would do it.\r\nAlso if you give score to a collection without commenting it, would be nice if an empty comment would not be shown.\r\nSome sort of multiple collection upload would be nice, or maybe atleast the possibility of first uploading a collection and then coming to a view where the file_id.diz shows so that you could pretty much spy the colly info from there.',7,NULL,NULL),(154,'dipswitch',1258911443,'yeah nup, batch upload is a good idea. spot, you can kinda spy on an execution of this idea if you register on www.streetfiles.org and try to upload a batch of graff fotos. first the upload gets proceeded, and then you can edit the whole bunch.',7,'Last edited by dipswitch 2009-11-22 18:37',NULL),(155,'dipswitch',1258912584,'what do you need these file_id logos for? ',37,NULL,NULL),(156,'yonx',1258923759,'for the ascii-kÃ¥seri-corner?',34,NULL,NULL),(157,'yonx',1258923840,'the sidebarlinks to the magz are broken!',6,NULL,NULL),(158,'dMG',1258930005,'for a future ascii article section :D',34,NULL,NULL),(160,'dMG',1258930605,'Design change: Add Comment at bottom of rendered colly (so that you don&#39;t have to scroll to top to add comment)\r\n',33,NULL,NULL),(161,'dMG',1258930669,'But it&#39;s a meal worthy a king! ',29,NULL,NULL),(182,'Spot',1258993735,'yupp, they are for the site. =)',37,NULL,NULL),(183,'dipswitch',1258994464,'the for prompt reply, i forwarded it to him.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nwould you be so kind and post the same stuff into http://www.pouet.net/topic.php?which=6666 - so people don&#39;t bitch senselessly.',40,NULL,NULL),(163,'dMG',1258932834,'I believe they are for the ascii apps section to make the filelist look good in bbs mode.\r\n',37,NULL,NULL),(164,'dMG',1258933027,'We&#39;ve been discussing a batch upload function already before. I think it&#39;s almost a must have and i think (but i dare not say it is certain) that it is in the site todo list already. Thanks for your inputs, guys. Keep em&#39; coming :)\r\n',7,NULL,NULL),(192,'dMG',1259004105,'Yes, it was main priority ;) ;)<br />\r\n',40,NULL,NULL),(476,'Spot',1260196484,'that will come.',122,NULL,NULL),(166,'dMG',1258938471,'Function to click on the number of comments on \"TOP COMMENTATORS\" to get a list of collys that certain user has commented on',33,NULL,NULL),(489,'ne7',1260310124,'quickie from me:<br />\r\nhttp://www.asciiarena.com/info_crew.php?crew=TW8mIzM5O1NvdWw=&sort_by=a.filename<br />\r\nif you look at mo&#39;soul&#39;s crew page you can see its claiming there are no members as well ^ odd eh? =)<br />\r\nandy',126,NULL,NULL),(169,'forsaken',1258942543,'Hey dmg, that incomplete one you were talking about was this one, right?\r\nhttp://artscene.textfiles.com/ascii/mortimer_twang/MortimerTwang2.txt\r\n\r\nJust making sure.\r\n\r\nNo luck when searching for KaU, btw.',31,'Last edited by forsaken 2009-11-23 03:16',NULL),(170,'forsaken',1258942750,'Yeah, I could tell...well, messes are fixable anyway and I don&#39;t mind either way.',38,NULL,NULL),(171,'yonx',1258967996,'where did the add-comment-button positioned below the colly go? :C',32,NULL,NULL),(530,'flower',1260586887,'Hey,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLooking for some ascii for the following sections:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\"Nintendo\" (alternatively Nintendo DS, or NDS)<br />\r\n\"IPhone\"<br />\r\n\"PC\"       (any alternative here, but nothing with IBM in it :) )<br />\r\n\"PSP\"      (alternatively Playstation Portable)<br />\r\n\"Requests\"<br />\r\n\"Archives\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIt can be request, or suggestions to some cool collies that already has this inside - yes, excuse me, I am a little lazy to browse through the 1000&#39;s available here :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCheers,<br />\r\nFlo',137,NULL,NULL),(531,'Spot',1260638965,'are you running a board?',137,NULL,NULL),(532,'dipswitch',1260669195,'here&#39;s one, more to come later perhaps.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://dipswitch.untergrund.net/iphone.txt',137,NULL,NULL),(177,'dipswitch',1258987366,'ah, okay! since the site brought me in such ascii mood, i might actually do some of those! =)',37,NULL,NULL),(178,'dipswitch',1258987626,'\r\nsorry if i cause bad feeling when i ask - but why exactly does the site need to be for firefox 3.5 only? i installed it immediately because i was so on fire to see this one - but many people do not use firefox for diverse reasons, and rightfully complain. what kind of technique requires firefox 3.5 like that? is there no option for a \"light version\"?',40,NULL,NULL),(180,'dipswitch',1258990686,'concerning this, i got a bug report from an old pal:\r\n\r\n\"Shit man that site gives me an error when I use Firefox 3.5.5.  Tells me I need Firefox 3.5... Guess it&#39;s because I run Linux?\"',40,NULL,NULL),(181,'Spot',1258991679,'it also works with IE 7 and 8, and Opera 10.\r\n\r\nHe is probably using some plugin/script that messes up the user agent stuff.\r\nIt happened to dMG as well.\r\n\r\nWe have tested this in FF on Linux/MacOS and Windows without problems.\r\n\r\nWhy it needs recent browsers? The lovely Topaz you are looking at right now\r\nwouldn&#39;t work otherwize and the site is designed around it.\r\nAnd it is only possible to embed fonts with the latest versions of the browsers.\r\n\r\nCutting edge has a price ;)',40,NULL,NULL),(184,'Black Jack',1258995498,'I&#39;m dipswitch&#39;s \"old pal\" :P<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSpot was absolutely right.  I use Tor+Privoxy from time-to-time and it had permanently modified my UserAgent to some kind of Firefox 3.0.7 on NT nonsense.  Anyway it&#39;s all fixed and the site looks great!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs a fellow web developer, I absolutely agree with Spot about using latest browsers.  A cutting edge site should enjoy all the benefits of using browsers that actually support the newer standards.  (keyword: standards)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOn that note, though, I usually use Chromium myself, but I&#39;m willing to load up ol&#39; FF for this beautiful site until Google gets their shit together.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGreat work Spot, I look forward to checking the entire thing out!  So far so good!',40,NULL,NULL),(185,'Sir Garbagetru',1258999874,'well it might have been fixed before I caused massive issues by having too long a name (:',5,NULL,NULL),(193,'dMG',1259004767,'http://www.asciiarena.com/apps.php?sort_by=name<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFirst 2 entries have wrong bg color',32,NULL,NULL),(187,'SGtrUck',1259000483,'DMG and Ziphoid know if it doens&#39;t work in Opera, I get all pissy (:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n',40,NULL,NULL),(194,'dMG',1259004821,'When hitting Reply on a post, the cursor should be positioned on the reply window. Now i need to scroll down the entire post before i can reply.<br />\r\n',32,NULL,NULL),(195,'Spot',1259005049,'nice to hear, and thanx for the compliments! =) this is my first coding project ever, so hearing that people likes it, feels very good! i will try to fix all issues as we go!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nedit: i posted on pouet as well.',40,'Last edited by Spot 2009-11-23 20:38',NULL),(189,'SGtrUck',1259002546,'It&#39;s time for \"Truck spams about some compo he may forget to upload the results from\" (actually, I _will_ upload the results from BP/Outline/etc here, cuz, well, I can and it would be good to have that stuff online.  People ask about it... oh I&#39;m spamming right.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSPAM:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFINNISH AMIGA GROUP (FAG) is having the biggest Amiga-only party in Finland this year - FAP (Finnish Amiga Party.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://low.fi/~nosfe/fap2009/compos.php<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou will notice that there is an ASCII compo there.  And since it&#39;s an Amiga party, you can guarantee your colly / entry will be shown on REAL HARDWARE.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou also can enter some other thing if you want.  Heck you can even show up.  FAG would like you to show up.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSo, ya know, right before you start working on your colly for Datastorm, try some stuff out for the FAG ascii compo (:',41,NULL,NULL),(190,'dMG',1259003834,'nope that&#39;s not it. Like i said, it&#39;s HOS-CIC5.LHA<br />\r\n',31,NULL,NULL),(579,'Spot',1261365649,'aSBoYXZlIHRha2VuIGNhcmUgb2YgYSBsb2Ygb2Ygc3R1ZmYgaW4gdGhlIHBvaW50cyBzeXN0ZW0sDQphbmQgZ3JvdXBzL2FydGlzdHMgYXJlIG9ubHkgc3VwcG9zZWQgdG8gZ2V0IHJhbmtlZCBpZiB0aGV5IGhhdmUgMyB2b3RlcyBvciBtb3JlLA0KYnV0IGl0IGRvZXNuJ3Qgc2VlbSB0byB3b3JrIGFzIGl0IHNob3VsZC4uIGFuZCBpIGRvbid0IGtub3cgdGhlIHJlYXNvbiB5ZXQu',103,NULL,1),(201,'forsaken',1259007038,'The website is actually coded quite well and the design is great. Also what dmg said.',40,NULL,NULL),(202,'ansichrist',1259007735,'MMkay.',41,NULL,NULL),(203,'skope',1259009393,'Finnish Amiga Group probably has the best acronym ever. Well initials in this case I guess...',41,NULL,NULL),(204,'dMG',1259011604,'If the official party tee will say *fap* *fap* *fap*, sign me up for one at once!',41,NULL,NULL),(205,'forsaken',1259012402,'add a file_id.diz to a colly after you&#39;ve uploaded it already? I don&#39;t think you can but just wondering.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI&#39;d like this file_id.diz:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n--------------------------------------------<br />\r\ne^D     e p s i l o n   d e s i g n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n            a s c i i d r e a m s         cG<br />\r\n--------------------------------------------<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nadded to Ascii Dreams Collection, which I uploaded yesterday.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(crap, forum formatting messed the file_id.diz up a bit but you know what I mean)',42,'Last edited by forsaken 2009-11-23 22:41',NULL),(206,'dalezy',1259012752,'i&#39;d like to have one that says \"dalezy\" (for my page over at http://dlz.1mhz.org)<br />\r\ni already got one from dipswitch, but i want those to be in rotation! :D',22,NULL,NULL),(207,'dalezy',1259014087,'anyone know of a surefire way getting ff3.5 to work with ubuntu (hardy)? i can only watch that site on my slower windows box, which rend