ana-nana-naaaaanaaaa ;)',57,NULL,NULL),(283,'dipswitch',1259234777,'<br />\r\ni was about to upload the colly tG!.CLAW.TXT - and was warned by this error msg:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis filetype is not allowed here!<br />\r\nInform an Admin if this is a valid colly! <br />\r\n<br />\r\ni guess its because of the fullstop in the filename? but there are many original colly filenames like that! what should we do?',71,NULL,NULL),(285,'yonx',1259237061,'would be better to check if the file is binary or ascii rather than checking the filename.. the asciiscene must be the worst one ever regarding standards of filenames, i&#39;ve seen so many weird ones now :)',71,NULL,NULL),(286,'dMG',1259238227,'i noticed the same thing in another colly. It is because of more than one punctuations in the filename.<br />\r\n',71,NULL,NULL),(288,'yonx',1259239580,'it would be cool with a page describing what ascii is all about with perhaps some history-timeline linking to important collys (style definitions), for people who are not into the scene which might visit the page.. my knowledge about it is too weak to do anything, but if anyone has the guts it would be wikkid :) ',72,'Last edited by yonx 2009-11-26 13:47',NULL),(290,'dMG',1259243537,'Why would you want a sig that says skope? :D',57,NULL,NULL),(291,'skope',1259244134,'because of my handsomeness (there was an ascii heart here but they are apparently illegal now :~C',57,'Last edited by skope 2009-11-26 15:03',NULL),(292,'dlz',1259251551,'thanks dip =) so that&#39;s 2 from dip and 1 from ne7 now i got to figure how to implent ansilove (or go easy and just let things randomly rotate)',22,NULL,NULL),(590,'ne7',1261380190,'',147,NULL,1),(675,'Spot',1261827418,'KiB2YXJpb3VzIHNtYWxsIGZpeGVzDQoqIGkgZGVjaWRlZCBub3QgdG8gaW1wbGVtZW50IGZpbGUgcmVwbGFjZSwgaXQncyBhIHRvbyBiaWcgdGFzayBmb3IgbGl0dGxlIGdhaW4uIGNvbGx5cyBjYW4gYmUgcmUtcmVuZGVyZWQgYXMgaXQgaXMuIHJlcGxhY2luZyBmaWxlcyBjYW4gYmUgZG9uZSBieSBkZWxldGluZyBhIGNvbGx5IGFuZCByZXVwbG9hZGluZy4=',145,NULL,1),(589,'Spot',1261379576,'aXMgYWN0aW5nIHdlaXJkLi4uIHlva2kgaXQncyB5b3VyIGRiIHF1ZXJ5LCBpIG5lZWQgeW91ciBoZWxwIG9uIHRoaXMgb25lLiA9KQ0K',151,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 08:16',1),(295,'winden',1259266704,'Latest Chrome beta v4.0.249 on OSX is showing everything in topaz for me...',40,NULL,NULL),(296,'Spot',1259270508,'Hey that&#39;s great news! <br />\r\nCan you upload a grab somewhere?<br />\r\nI am curious on how the antialising looks.',40,NULL,NULL),(298,'winden',1259275956,'Sure, I&#39;ve uploaded a PNG capture to<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://picasaweb.google.com/lh/photo/ouTTHa1KMramdb1Sx5uMVA?feat=directlink<br />\r\n',40,NULL,NULL),(493,'Spot',1260325903,'i bet there ain&#39;t any ascii history in freax..<br />\r\nwell... sooner or later the legends will find their way here... let&#39;s jump them when that happens =)',72,NULL,NULL),(302,'Spot',1259284992,'dip, write it! ;)',72,NULL,NULL),(304,'dMG',1259285201,'haha yea dip is truly the man for the job',72,NULL,NULL),(459,'zorro',1260091262,'irc channel / eggdrop announcement of new collies/posts etc. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nyes/no? <br />\r\n<br />\r\ncheers,<br />\r\n2o',120,NULL,NULL),(465,'Spot',1260156327,'collys can now be reported broken. and broken collys can be viewed in the admin panel.<br />\r\n',122,NULL,NULL),(308,'dipswitch',1259289434,'oh my... puuuh. that is really a hard task to do. dunno when i will feel like it. but i might do it at some point.',72,NULL,NULL),(492,'Spot',1260325809,'where would we want the aka&#39;s to be displayed though?<br />\r\nthe release info field could get quite cluttered with schizofrenic girls like mortimer twang who has a million handles..',101,NULL,NULL),(551,'ne7',1260980983,'nice stuff dipswitch! \\o/',119,NULL,NULL),(554,'deathr0w',1260995743,'I am looking for a complete set of menus from entropy so if anyone can help let me know by a message then i&#39;ll let you know what i need.',119,NULL,NULL),(555,'dipswitch',1261048018,'hey deathrow, i think it would be better if you&#39;d open a new thread. and also list up what logos exactly you do need. cheers!',119,NULL,NULL),(556,'ne7',1261052656,'WendyBurton - i deleted her... Wendy@tube8.com = email addy',143,'Last edited by ne7 2009-12-17 13:27',NULL),(314,'SGtrUck',1259300914,'When using the forum, if you type the < followed by the - it appears to cut off the remaining text.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAt least when editing messages. Thus this test, which uses a &#39;reply.&#39;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAfter this next break there will be 10 numbers then < then - then some crap.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1234567890<br />\r\n<br />\r\n[edit] Yup, it definately cut off everything after the < and the -, no space needed, just type < and then - and WHAM the message gets truncated.',48,'Last edited by SGtrUck 2009-11-27 06:49',NULL),(316,'yonx',1259315171,'just show the 1st newsitem on frontpage and add a \"older news\"-link to prevent the frontpage fromm turning into a blog :)',81,'Last edited by yonx 2009-11-27 10:46',NULL),(317,'SGtrUck',1259316213,'Just cuz it may not make any sense in my crap bug report that turned out to not be a bug report:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe site looks awesome in OWB, which _does_ have support for embedded fonts.  And also in Arora, which also has support for embedded fonts.  I&#39;d say any NEW build of a webkit browser will show the site as it is intended.  (Latest iPhone/iPod Touch doesn&#39;t.  And I&#39;m using OWB 1.5 ... latest.)<br />\r\n',40,NULL,NULL),(318,'yonx',1259316680,'seems the aa in chrome/osx is as bad as in the other browsers.. i wonder if they removed the aa-curse in snow leopard',40,NULL,NULL),(319,'dipswitch',1259316822,'yes, i was about to suggest that as well!',81,NULL,NULL),(320,'dipswitch',1259317061,'<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni think it would be a cool idea to have a textmode ad, like a bbs -- not to spam the collies with it though (heaven forbid), but to post messages in the remaining bbs&#39;s to attract some more related people, and also to use in our own ascii collies.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni could layout one, but then i could use only my logos because i dont have the other ones as ascii, only as png. spot, any way you can access the other ascii arena logos as text?',82,NULL,NULL),(321,'yonx',1259317504,'i am all for spamming the collys as well, atleast new releases :)',82,NULL,NULL),(322,'dMG',1259319081,'',83,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-26 12:38',1),(325,'dMG',1259319458,'also on top of posts, not only bottom',85,NULL,NULL),(326,'yonx',1259319464,'the votingsystem, or rather the calculating of ranking, as it is now is a bit flawed (imho) since popular collys tend to get lower ranks than non-popular.. <br />\r\nthree people voting 10 on a colly would place higher than 100 people voting 10 on a colly with 1 man voting a 9 :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\na method to weight the ranking to be more fair is the bayesian method:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nb / (b+m)) Ã— S + (m / (b+m)) Ã— A<br />\r\n<br />\r\nS = the average score<br />\r\nb = numbers of votes<br />\r\nm = minimum amount of votes (it is now set to 3 which is very low)<br />\r\nA = average score for the whole database<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(right now  the cursor is outside the screen and i cant see what i am writing, so sorry for any typos :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthis way of ranking the collys ensures that the collys with most high votes are placed over collys with fewer high votes, rather than just calculating a simple average. ',86,NULL,NULL),(327,'yonx',1259319538,'the auto-linefeed is damn annoying :(',86,NULL,NULL),(328,'yonx',1259319884,'i also noticed it generates a second page to quick, when the 1st page is full but not overflowing, resulting in a empty page 2.. should easily be fixed with a \"+1\" somewhere in the paginating-code..<br />\r\n<br />\r\nalso, PAGE 1 OF 2 looks so ugly, i rather see the usual <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1 2 3 4 5 6 ... with the current page highlighted',85,NULL,NULL),(330,'yonx',1259320161,'the linefeed makes the formula a bit hard to read so i try again here: b / (b+m)) * S + (m / (b+m)) * A. what the formula does is to weight collys with few votes towards the site-average..',86,NULL,NULL),(624,'dMG',1261459194,'SSBqdXN0IHBpY3R1cmUgaXQgdGhhdCB0aGVyZSB3aWxsIGJlIHRvbyBmZXcgY29udHJpYnV0aW9ucyBpZiBoZWxkIGV2ZXJ5IHdlZWssIHRoYXQncyBhbGwuDQo=',154,NULL,1),(623,'Spot',1261459093,'',154,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-22 06:18',1),(547,'SGtrUck',1260914986,'Well, here&#39;s 2 descriptions of twattage that I&#39;ve heard, which sum up why I use it despite it being a newfangled buzzwordy thing:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. My friend Andr00, describing twitter:<br />\r\n  \"Twitter is like signing up for sms&#39;s from cool people.\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Dalezy, on what he likes about Twitter:<br />\r\n  \"It&#39;s sort of like calling a bbs and getting all the new posts.\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIt&#39;s kinda, overall, basic, straight up communication between folks.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTo see what it would look like if we used it like an rss feed, just, a LOT more spammy:<br />\r\nhttp://twitter.com/nectarineradio<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(I asked if folks would want us to do this with Scenesat and the answer came back \"um, not really. It&#39;s why I don&#39;t follow nectarine that way.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBut it WOULD work for us, and the api is pretty freaking simple from what I understand.  (I think it&#39;s an http post with &#39;username&#39; and &#39;password&#39; fields, and that&#39;s IT.  Oh and it has to be less than 140 chars.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n',120,NULL,NULL),(335,'SGtrUck',1259335171,'The [Prev] [Next] [Last] buttons do not work if you use [Prev] on page 2, such as, well, this post.  (Opera 10.10)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnd \"do not work\" means you do not see any posts in the thread anymore, just that there are multiple pages.',48,NULL,NULL),(336,'hAkR!',1259351314,'our remote contribution to the bootblockintro compo at the FAP is on the way...',41,NULL,NULL),(337,'cG',1259356638,'If the fags are calling, one *must* step up!',41,NULL,NULL),(576,'Spot',1261361113,'KiBmaXhlZCBzb3J0IGJ5IGluIGFydGlzdCBpbmZvDQoqIGZpeGVkIHRoZSBwcml2YXRlIG1haWwgc3lzdGVtLCBpdCdzIG5vdCBwZXJmZWN0LCBidXQgYXRsZWFzdCBpdCB3b3Jrcy4NCg==',145,NULL,1),(513,'yonx',1260530339,'since all fishermen are free on Mondays it would be logical to have deadline on the first Monday in each month. It&#39;s the same day as the enemy aircraft alarm testing goes off in Sweden as well, it&#39;s a good reminder! ',124,NULL,NULL),(340,'Spot',1259433525,'O_O they stole our bblock intro compo! :P',41,NULL,NULL),(341,'Spot',1259443546,'bump!<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni want to see this colly!<br />\r\n',57,NULL,NULL),(517,'dino',1260533616,'what about making this as said in the \"....\" post, <br />\r\na dS! collection together to release on DATASTORM 2010<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthe question is if you think it&#39;s a good thing, and if so what the THEME should be ?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nall I can come up with is to take the list of CREWS here at asciiarena and make <br />\r\nthem all together, yeah. alot, but we should handle that, yes ???<br />\r\n<br />\r\n',133,NULL,NULL),(511,'yonx',1260529800,'exactly, one artist entry for each handle, linked to all other handles.. that&#39;s how it&#39;s usually done at www.discogs.com or other similar sites..',101,NULL,NULL),(346,'Spot',1259463136,'the oldest ascii colly i have seen is from the end of 1992.<br />\r\nwhen did the colly thing start? which one is the oldest you know?<br />\r\nupload it!',91,NULL,NULL),(347,'Spot',1259475966,'nod.',82,NULL,NULL),(504,'dMG',1260526458,'I don&#39;t understand what you mean. It&#39;s hardly likely that someone adds a Mark Ryder colly as Terminal Silence f.i. and the dupecheck takes care of the submission bit.',101,NULL,NULL),(572,'Spot',1261274219,'KiBhZG1pbnMgY2FuIG5vdyBlZGl0IGZvcnVtIHBvc3QgdG9waWNzIHZpYSB0aGUgZWRpdCBidXR0b24u',145,NULL,1),(679,'nerv',1261875244,'',147,'Last edited by nerv 2009-12-27 01:54',1),(508,'Spot',1260528270,'you mean quoting?',83,NULL,NULL),(510,'dMG',1260529087,'i guess i do',83,NULL,NULL),(351,'hAkR!',1259501226,'hi mates, i`m looking for some AS(ii/ANSi logos, so here it is:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. file_id.diz say \"Y-CREW\"<br />\r\n2. logo`s saying \"YCREW\" & \"hAkRi\"<br />\r\n3. lastly a colored BBS logo saying \"Blast from the Past\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthx in advance!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhAkR!',94,'Last edited by hAkR! 2009-11-29 14:27',NULL),(575,'Spot',1261356020,'YXMgeW91IG1pZ2h0IGhhdmUgbm90aWNlZCwgdGhpcyBpcyBhY3RpdmF0ZWQgb24gdGhlIGxpdmUgc2l0ZSBub3cuIGVuam95IQ0K',146,NULL,1),(354,'yonx',1259525737,'in messages and comments: convert anything starting with http:// to a link',96,NULL,NULL),(355,'Spot',1259528424,'http://www.asciiarena.com/info_release.php?filename=VFIhLVRSVUUudHh0<br />\r\n<br />\r\nwe should fix the colly, upload it, and then replace the .txt version with the original<br />\r\none. it has a screenclear before the sulk city logo.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni will make a \"report broken colly\" button, that makes a post to this thread with<br />\r\nthe broken colly, and a comment from the user.<br />\r\n',97,'Last edited by Spot 2009-11-29 22:02',NULL),(356,'Spot',1259528854,'omg! O_O he bypassed the &#39;official&#39; signature editor and made an ansi sig! :D<br />\r\n',94,'Last edited by Spot 2009-11-29 22:07',NULL),(523,'diNO',1260535095,'outside would be fair. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nI will also make a collection for the compo, so....<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI just think it would be neat of us to release something major like that,<br />\r\nI was looking at the list and figured it WASNT impossible to make them all <br />\r\n(the CREWS)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nbut, maybe i&#39;m the only one to think that,<br />\r\n<br />\r\n?',133,NULL,NULL),(503,'Spot',1260521847,'this could lead to some confusion though..<br />\r\npeople will add artists more than one time, under different handles,<br />\r\nand collys will be submitted with different handles.',101,NULL,NULL),(365,'SGtrUck',1259542706,'- The following is fucking LONG.  You may want to get a beer before starting to read. Or a spliff, if that&#39;s your thing. -<br />\r\n<br />\r\nA few of you may remember back before the MAIN party in France, there was discussion of having a ascii compo on the F*N HUGE screen.  That got shot down due to the limitations of the side panels (they didn&#39;t have the resolution to properly display a colly, especially since the center panel DID and you&#39;d have this... it wasn&#39;t gonna work.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSo we decided \"screw it, we&#39;re doing a demo that has a &#39;long&#39; colly in it. We haven&#39;t seen that.\"  (Obviously certain people looking for collys in the other area weren&#39;t around to talk about collys that did that, but it doesn&#39;t matter, because it&#39;s rare anyway.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSo folks signed up to do \"traincars\" - which would be 400x25 sections of \"train\" which would be displayed scrolling in the demo.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere were discussions of \"how\" to do this, and some confusion as to just exactly how we&#39;d deal with &#39;windows&#39; and such, and some folks WANTED that and others just were having enough creative stuff with a 400x25 area.  We discovered there is a bug in TextMate that will not allow 400x25 stuff.  Emacs _will_ do it, but seriously I don&#39;t think anyone besides myself is insane enough to do that.  CED obviously will, and I think there are enough of us here that can get you set up with your copy of CED that you have on your Amiga there.  That one.  There.  See?  Yes that one.  Ok now that we&#39;re clear that you have a copy of CED that you purchased, right there...<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnyway.  We had to cancel it at the party due to Irokos/Titan&#39;s grandmother dying, and he would not be able to make the party.  Now while Irokos does BLOCK - as does Malodix - they actually are helpful in this regard as we are using Block/Ansi for the background/foreground (what the trains are travelling thru.)  Also I only had one completed car - heck Dipswitch wasn&#39;t even able to do it right then due to moving, and his computer wasn&#39;t working properly.  Which I fixed, hopefully it&#39;s working well still (:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOh and we have music, I have that from T101, and it&#39;s not metal.  It fits, in an odd way.  At least I think it does.  When we get closer to completion maybe we get something else in there but I think this will work.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnyway this post is to say the project is NOT dead.  At all.  It hasn&#39;t really been touched lately, cept at Kindergarden where I worked with the &#39;engine&#39; a bit, and I do have FAP productions and stuff to do before Datastorm.  And this isn&#39;t a Datastorm production.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBut this _is_ a project that we&#39;re doing, collctively, and since no one had brought it up lately I thought I&#39;d better say: NO, not dead.  Still doing it.  PROBABLY for MAIN next year, but perhaps for another party - maybe Outline?  We&#39;ll discuss when we get more completed works in.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSo basically - here&#39;s the deal for what you need to do if you&#39;re doing a &#39;traincar&#39; -<br />\r\n<br />\r\nASCII, 400 x 25.  P0t-nOodle.  You can of course edit in Microknight or Topaz, but it will be displayed in P0t-nOodle so you should be sure it looks the way you want in P0t-nOodle.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou&#39;ll also be doing a &#39;shared&#39; car with everyone else in the production, tagging your name or whatever.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- optional, \"hey I wanna do summat else too\" stuff below.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSign up if you&#39;re still doing one, or if you want to do one having heard about this NOW, or having time NOW.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Notes:<br />\r\n1. You can do light on dark -or- dark on light.  If you do dark on light, it will be displayed \"outside.\"  This is the NORMAL way we&#39;ll have it, and I figure most folks will do it that way.  However, if you wish to do light on dark - as in the stuff in the asciiarena header - it will be displayed in a TUNNEL.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Irokos and Malodix are doing the backgrounds/foregrounds in block/ansi for us, if you want to help out on that, let me know here as well.  We need cityscapes, tunnel bricks, \"city people walking about,\" \"trees,\" \"telephone poles,\" \"bridges\" and whatnot, stuff that will form the landscape the train goes thru.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. I think it was Zaner who was wanting to do his ascii over the TOP of an actual car graphic, as in \"we may need a frame to work within, with windows.\"<br />\r\nI do like this idea but it has 2 issues I see:<br />\r\n A> no car graphic is the size we need, and blowing one up didn&#39;t really work... so someone needs to draw one.<br />\r\n B> I know of _no_ editors that let you put a background behind your text.  Now maybe we need to write one for this.  I dunno.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. I do not know how we&#39;re doing the &#39;shared&#39; car yet.  Prolly set up a... I dunno, a shared edit thing on the web.  That may end up being what we do anyway, since, well, that way we can put the backdrops up, etc.  But that will be coding that I&#39;m gonna have to do after FAP and ... well I have ... projects... man I just need to figure out how to get shit DONE.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. I&#39;m SURE there&#39;s something else.  Beyond the whole \"editor won&#39;t let me do 400x25\" issue.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- So far, I have abho&#39;s car (:  Others signed up and were maybe working on things but didn&#39;t get &#39;em done.  Just reminding you - project isn&#39;t dead (:<br />\r\n',98,'Last edited by SGtrUck 2009-11-30 01:59',NULL),(366,'SGtrUck',1259544313,'heh there haven&#39;t been enough bootblock intro compos lately... only the Atari people ):  Time to fix that...<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHey wait, when did we get the ability to do multiple colors in our tags? Crap, I need to ... make one ugly ass thing and be reminded that I need a clue before I do that.',41,NULL,NULL),(367,'SGtrUck',1259544340,'Mail section doens&#39;t work at all (Opera 10.10)',48,NULL,NULL),(368,'SGtrUck',1259544509,'     _____     _______ _______ ___     _______ _______ ___ ___      ___<br />\r\n   Â¯Â¯Â¯ __    /Â¯Â¯     /Â¯Â¯     /Â¯Â¯ /   /Â¯Â¯     /Â¯Â¯     /Â¯Â¯ /Â¯Â¯ /   Â¯Â¯Â¯Â¯<br />\r\n _   Â¯Â¯Â¯    / __ /  / __ /  /   /___/       /       /   /   /  ___<br />\r\n  ____     /   Â¯Â¯  /   Â¯Â¯  /    Â¯Â¯Â¯/    Â¯Â¯Â¯Z___    /___    /     Â¯Â¯Â¯<br />\r\nÂ¯Â¯Â¯ ___   /       /    /  /       /    ___/    ___/ Â¯Â¯/   /   __<br />\r\n   Â¯  Â¯Â¯ /       /    /  /       /    Â¯Â¯ /    Â¯Â¯ /   /   /  Â¯Â¯Â¯ ___<br />\r\n   ___  /_______/____/__/_______/_______/_______/   /___/    ___ Â¯Â¯Â¯ <br />\r\n  Â¯Â¯          Â¯Â¯    Â¯  Â¯     Â¯Â¯Â¯     Â¯Â¯Â¯      Â¯Â¯      Â¯Â¯    Â¯Â¯Â¯<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHmm yes that looks slightly better dark on light. Or wait, no, hmm, odd... Textmate has gaps between the chars, so this loses the &#39;stutter-shaking&#39; effect that sort of made it look slightly less crap.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAh well I&#39;ll go fix something for DDT now he only bitched about it 4 hours ago (:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDarn it, still can&#39;t paste &#39;em here. Shit. Ok well here: http://pastebin.ca/1693318',22,'Last edited by SGtrUck 2009-11-30 02:29',NULL),(369,'yonx',1259545515,'sounds like a fucking wicked project!! <br />\r\n',98,NULL,NULL),(370,'Spot',1259546076,'so... did i get this right? it will be released in a year?<br />\r\nif you write a short version of this and link to this thread you can post it as news as well.. click upload to post news.',98,NULL,NULL),(372,'zANEr',1259564783,'I&#39;ve discovered a bug on the Artists Page.<br />\r\nIt tells you there are 2 pages only, and the 2nd page ends with artists letter S.<br />\r\nHowever if I search for myself I can find myself, but not on the list because it stops at S.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGreat job!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIt&#39;s like a web-bbs-ascii-arena-madness, much love.',48,NULL,NULL),(373,'zANEr',1259565409,'I&#39;m happily taking ascii requests for FILE_ID.DIZ usage, if you need anything fresh for your releases hit me up.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPossibly I will also draw logos but it depends for which purpose and if I like my result if I attempt to do it ;)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSOME RECENT DRAWINGS FOR YOU PLEASURE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n( I intended to paste some examples here, but the spaces get removed, when the bug is fixed I will post some )<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCheers,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nzNr/dS! - TY!BBS<br />\r\n',99,'Last edited by zANEr 2009-11-30 08:18',NULL),(375,'hAkR!',1259571338,'hehe, pls draw a file_id.diz for \"Y-Crew\", thx...',99,NULL,NULL),(376,'SGtrUck',1259571993,'Actually, \"a year\" seems like too long, but I throw that out to y&#39;all who are doing cars.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe _do_ want to get a version running on the HUGE F*N SCREEN at MAIN, but first I wanna have a tested, running version (:  Especially since I don&#39;t really code Windows stuff (:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLet me try to write up a succinct version of this... yeah, it SHOULD go on the news.',98,NULL,NULL),(543,'Spot',1260853719,'heh :D i meant a BBS.',137,NULL,NULL),(544,'Spot',1260854878,'aSB0cmllZCByZXVwbG9hZGluZyBpdCBub3cuDQpkaWRuJ3Qgd29yay4gaSBkaWQgc29tZSBmaXhlcyBpbiB0aGUgY29kZS4gc3RpbGwgZGlkbid0IHdvcmsuDQpncnIuIHN0aWxsIGxvb2tpbmcgaW50byBpdC4=',139,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 04:27',1),(379,'nUP!',1259583234,'Shapechanger and also Supertouch did some nice ones too.',30,'Last edited by nUP! 2009-11-30 13:35',NULL),(380,'dMG',1259585899,'splat = desoto<br />\r\nterminal silence = mark ryder<br />\r\nnup = b<br />\r\n<br />\r\nand so on.. you get the point ;)',101,NULL,NULL),(382,'yonx',1259594771,'remember that the Group you submit for the colly is the group which released the colly, not the groups the artist is member of.. ',102,NULL,NULL),(515,'dino',1260532552,'super nice!! <br />\r\n<br />\r\nthis is the best thing happening, all together I mean, ascii arena, AND internal forum.<br />\r\nthanks alot, you made me look 15 years younger allready. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nhopefully I will blast DATASTORM with a collection, <br />\r\n<br />\r\nBUT ! shouldnt we make a dS! collection TOGETHER aswell ???? <br />\r\na couple of logos each shouldn&#39;t be so much of a hussle should it ?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI think the THEME of the collection is then the main problem, <br />\r\nwhat should it be about, or what kind of logos should we focus on ?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhave a nice day,<br />\r\n<br />\r\ndiNO/dS!',65,NULL,NULL),(534,'ne7',1260716689,'d&r_ecol.txt ',139,NULL,NULL),(388,'yonx',1259603380,'',103,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 04:18',1),(389,'ne7',1259610071,'eWVzIGhhZCBub3RpY2VkIHRoYXQgaGVoZSAtIG11c3Qgc2F5IG5pY2Ugb25lIHRvIHNwb3QgbiBkbWcgbiB0aGUgbGFkcyB0aG8gdGhlIHNpdGUNCmlzIGxvb2tpbmcgYmxvb2R5IGFjZSAtIGEgZmV3IGxpdHRsZSBidWdzIGJ1dCBpdHMgaXRzIHJvY2tpbmcgYWxvbmcgdmVyeSBuaWNlbHkgDQoNCmFuZHk=',103,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 04:18',1),(390,'dipswitch',1259610599,'which ones have been submitted wrongly like that?',102,NULL,NULL),(391,'Spot',1259610671,'i hope you fixed it when you saw it yonxer?<br />\r\n',102,NULL,NULL),(542,'flower',1260848737,'dipswitch: Thanks! looking out for more to come :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSpot: I used to run skateboarding yes, not so much anymore though.',137,NULL,NULL),(535,'dipswitch',1260719301,'<br />\r\ni just want to bring to your attention the very neat project by pandur/blackmaiden - an online ansi drawing platform which is more pc-scene based, but also has amiga fonts.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n>>>>>> http://ansi.drastic.net/',140,NULL,NULL),(591,'ne7',1261380257,'',147,NULL,1),(458,'zorro',1260089506,'1) 80*XXX saying either DOOMS DAY MACHINE or just DDM<br />\r\n   dividers for last callers, oneliners and new dir would be awesome<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) 80*XXX saying STRANGE CARG0<br />\r\n <br />\r\n3) 80*30(+/-) saying \"This file passed ... DARKSTAR 84\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthanks,<br />\r\n2o',119,'Last edited by zorro 2009-12-06 09:55',NULL),(462,'Spot',1260143855,'you mean like hooking up a bot to the asciiarena db?<br />\r\ni&#39;d love that, but i have no experience with eggdrop.',120,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-07 00:58',NULL),(400,'Spot',1259611432,'should be doable.<br />\r\n',101,NULL,NULL),(402,'Spot',1259611902,'this should be possible i guess, but ... <br />\r\nwhat should the title of the link be then, the long ugly url?<br />\r\ni vote for \"Click Me\" or \"Link\"...',96,NULL,NULL),(403,'yonx',1259612924,'aSB2b3RlIGZvciB0aGUgZG9tYWlubmFtZSBsaW5rZWQgdG8uLg0KDQplZGl0OiBwZXJoYXBzIHdpdGhvdXQgdGhlIHd3dy4gYW5kIHRvcGRvbWFpbg0KDQpleGFtcGxlOg0KDQp0aGlzIGlzIGEgZnVja2luZyBuaWNlIHZpZGVvOiBodHRwOi8vd3d3LnlvdXR1YmUuY29tL2lkPWxpd2Zod29paGZxaTINCg0KPj4NCg0KdGhpcyBpcyBhIGZ1Y2tpbmcgbmljZSB2aWRlbzogW3lvdXR1YmVd',96,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-28 13:40',1),(404,'dipswitch',1259617416,'okay, can i have some logos then? =)<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni dont want to be that unmodest that i use my own. i regard, for example, dmg&#39;s green log much better than mine. can someone make me have it in text format?',82,NULL,NULL),(486,'yonx',1260270385,'the \"More news\"-link is only visible when i am not logged in..',81,NULL,NULL),(406,'Spot',1259631054,'http://www.asciiarena.com/info_release.php?filename=YWwtd2FyIS50eHQ=<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthat one has some history info in it that could be used.',72,NULL,NULL),(407,'Spot',1259631170,'argh... i hate you. :P<br />\r\n',96,NULL,NULL),(408,'cG',1259659309,'\"seventy five percent\"<br />\r\nalt. \"75 percent\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\n80x??<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBring it on ;)',108,NULL,NULL),(409,'flower',1259661354,'It would be cool with some place to see all the submitted ascii arena logos :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCheers,<br />\r\nFlo',109,'Last edited by flower 2009-12-01 10:56',NULL),(410,'yonx',1259667888,'haha, we have to level up your PHP-knowledge for each excercise, no good staying on the same level too long!',96,NULL,NULL),(411,'yonx',1259668217,'it would have been great to hook up with some old dewds like that and make interviews for some kind of serious history-making attempt..<br />\r\n<br />\r\nis there any ascii-history in the freax-books? i still havent come around to buy those..',72,NULL,NULL),(412,'yonx',1259668601,'i didn&#39;t fix anything because i wasn&#39;t sure, but this one f.e looks like a independent release to me..<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://www.asciiarena.com/info_release.php?filename=LXN0IWFvdy50eHQ=<br />\r\n',102,'Last edited by yonx 2009-12-01 12:57',NULL),(413,'skope',1259677708,'Dunno what it is that pisses people off about the ascii scene but:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://www.vague.lorraine-design.com/articles/scene/04-ascii_sucks-.html<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIt seems we all get to stand in the way of his vomit cascade. It was fun reading tho. ;)',110,NULL,NULL),(414,'dipswitch',1259679106,'he should simply go and fuck himself, especially considering that he most likely has absolutely no clue about bbs&#39;s and the culture connected with it.',110,NULL,NULL),(415,'skope',1259680685,'I agree. Upon first reading it I thougt I should write him a respone like in the good old days, but then I just couldn&#39;t find the strength to even bother. I might extend a long, thick, veiny and juicy dick for him to choke on in my next colly tho.',110,NULL,NULL),(416,'cG',1259681479,'Meh, just make fun of him right back.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nhttp://www.gfxzone.org/party/symphony_2003/24bpp/01/slayer-returning_jesus.html<br />\r\n<br />\r\nlolol<br />\r\n',110,NULL,NULL),(417,'dMG',1259681722,'done',108,NULL,NULL),(418,'skope',1259681801,'@cG :D<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat a pic, \"not at all\" pretentious haha...<br />\r\n',110,NULL,NULL),(419,'dMG',1259682786,'When was this article written? :)',110,NULL,NULL),(420,'skope',1259683360,'It&#39;s from Vague issue 1 which was released in 2007.',110,NULL,NULL),(421,'dMG',1259683648,'jawesome. the guy is clueless :D',110,NULL,NULL),(422,'cG',1259686585,'Indeed it is! ;D',108,NULL,NULL),(454,'ansichrist',1259972175,'http://pastebin.com/m2e3d1830',109,NULL,NULL),(455,'yonx',1259977040,'the one below the colly/comments has been gone ever since the release of the arena for some reason? bring it back bejbi!',117,NULL,NULL),(424,'ne7',1259712535,'haha that guy so needs a dry slap :D <br />\r\n',110,NULL,NULL),(456,'Spot',1260053644,'yupp i will...<br />\r\ni removed it when i redesigned it .. as i didn&#39;t want to rewrite it twice.<br />\r\n',117,NULL,NULL),(426,'flower',1259722940,'\"Instead of releasing 40 ascii-collections   with   the  same  logos  repeated (sorry, each differs from one another, often with one char, but this is how they work out their own style), you&#39;d better just write one good article.\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\n.. it appears he failed in both :-)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe article is just a rant, no logic argument chain established in any of his dislikes.  Who knows what cute ascii-girl turned him down.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCheers,<br />\r\nFlo',110,NULL,NULL),(427,'cG',1259747471,'\" Who knows what cute ascii-girl turned him down.\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI&#39;m guessing DMG did!<br />\r\n',110,NULL,NULL),(428,'roodolph',1259749512,'What. the. fuck. and he&#39;s from Poland, like me :(',110,NULL,NULL),(429,'dipswitch',1259796417,'<br />\r\ni think it would make more sense that, when members of a group are displayed, then in the column \"releases\" only the releases for the particular group are counted, and not their releases in total.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nan extreme example: http://www.asciiarena.com/info_crew.php?crew=Die%20Kranken%20Bomber&sort_by=a.filename<br />\r\nit looks like i have been the moving active force behind dkb, suggested by the number of my releases, but it creates a totally wrong picture.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nyou get what i mean?',113,NULL,NULL),(430,'dMG',1259797400,'Should be smth like Releases N (Total: N) me thinks<br />\r\n',113,NULL,NULL),(431,'dipswitch',1259807746,'yes that sounds good!',113,NULL,NULL),(432,'SGtrUck',1259835582,'Roodolph: Fuc&#39;im up, son!<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(shame on a...)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nanyway he&#39;s had far too much attention paid to him, like the Pouet lamers.  Ignore him, he doesn&#39;t want to get it, and he will actively try to not get it just to try to piss someone off.  Let him waste his time, it&#39;s what he wants to do.',110,NULL,NULL),(433,'dipswitch',1259840868,'<br />\r\ni&#39;d like to have a full-size logo saying \"enough dubs\". needing it until the end of december. thanks!',114,NULL,NULL),(434,'dipswitch',1259840894,'oh and if i get more than one logo, it is even better =)',114,NULL,NULL),(435,'dMG',1259857031,'Whats a full-sized logo?',114,NULL,NULL),(436,'dipswitch',1259861528,'full-sized logo in the sense of \"not a file-id.diz\". up to 80 chars broad and whatever tall.',114,NULL,NULL),(437,'winden',1259875807,'I&#39;ve scavanged a bit on the internets for the antialiasing issue...<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLatest development Webkit supports a new CSS tag called -webkit-font-smoothing that allows disabling the antialias. Neither official Safari nor Chrome on Snow Leopard support it yet tho, but it would be good to add the tag so that it can be tested when it is released.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe bugs/examples are at http://trac.webkit.org/browser/trunk/LayoutTests/platform/mac/fast/css/font-smoothing-expected.png?rev=48441 and http://code.google.com/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=23270',40,NULL,NULL),(438,'Spot',1259882770,'do i smell a new dip colly?',114,NULL,NULL),(439,'Spot',1259882923,'hehe... i left him a little greeting in vague #2... i hope he finds us =)',110,NULL,NULL),(440,'Spot',1259883016,'INTERESTING!',40,NULL,NULL),(441,'dMG',1259887531,'done',114,NULL,NULL),(442,'dMG',1259887678,'i have my doubts about it doing anything in osx due to steve jobs&#39; hitlerish attitude regarding aa<br />\r\n',40,NULL,NULL),(496,'dMG',1260464217,'on the artist page perhaps. i&#39;ll try and figure out other places where it would be applicable',101,NULL,NULL),(444,'ne7',1259891491,'done n sent u a pm on here pal :)',114,NULL,NULL),(446,'dipswitch',1259892496,'thanks guys!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nno, it&#39;s not for a colly, but for an infofile of a forthcoming netlabel compilation.',114,NULL,NULL),(447,'ne7',1259892760,'hugs to ps too :) \\o/',114,NULL,NULL),(520,'Spot',1260534416,'oh man... that&#39;s shitloads... <br />\r\n<br />\r\ni have already made my compo ascii for the storm... will this be released outside the compo?',133,NULL,NULL),(522,'Spot',1260534513,'dMG does all registered members of dS have axx to this forum?<br />\r\nCan someone post a current ds memberlist?',135,NULL,NULL),(524,'dMG',1260537017,'i... dunno... how could i check :)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nand current list should be... like in dS!-dive.txt + you i guess? :)<br />\r\n',135,NULL,NULL),(527,'SGtrUck',1260545579,'I don&#39;t suppose we could get that as a twitter thing rather than an rss, and then use one of the twattage->rss things, killing 2 birds with one stone, eh?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCuz I&#39;d like to have a twattage thing (not in my main twattage list but you know a &#39;list&#39; thing you just sort of look at like an rss feed but it&#39;s in your twattage client.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCuz I don&#39;t do rss anymore, I use twattage.  And that way I&#39;d have it in irc AND Twattage for, ya know, the past week of stuff without having to filter on irc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI&#39;ll shut up now.',120,NULL,NULL),(528,'SGtrUck',1260545685,'I&#39;m good with Monday.  Because it won&#39;t really matter in the long run which day it is we use, that will _become_ the day to check after about 2 or 3 successful runs.  Point will be to HAVE successful runs (:',124,NULL,NULL),(529,'dMG',1260549308,'i&#39;ve never used twitter (and im fairly sure ill never will) so i have NO idea what you just said. But it sounds like there is a posibility to change twitter streams into rss so that sounds kinda nice... Question is, would it require extra coding in say an eggdrop to make it possible?<br />\r\n',120,NULL,NULL),(562,'Spot',1261173672,'',145,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 07:01',1),(585,'Spot',1261375775,'d2VsbC4uLiBtbW1tLi4gaXQgd2lsbCBuZWVkIHRvIGJlIGZpeGVkIHNvbWVob3cu',71,NULL,1),(586,'Spot',1261377439,'',145,NULL,1),(561,'deathr0w',1261165041,'',144,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 04:44',1),(563,'Spot',1261188861,'I have made som big ass and drastic changes to the forum/comments code.<br />\r\nIt is now 100% ascii+weird character friendly while remaining backwards compatible, so no old posts gets screwed.<br />\r\nThanx to ziphoid for some valuable input!<br />\r\nNone of this is implemented on the live site yet, all is on the dev site.<br />\r\nStay tuned! Soon we can rock it with ascii in the forum, and start compos<br />\r\nand co-op collys etc! :D',146,NULL,NULL),(608,'Spot',1261452026,'SG93IG9mdGVuIGRvIHdlIHdhbnQgY29tcG9zPw0KRXZlcnkgbW9uZGF5IG9yIG9uY2UgYSBtb250aD8NCldoYXQgdGhlbWUgc2hvdWxkIHRoZSBuZXh0IGNvbXBvIGJlIGFib3V0Pw0KSWYgd2UgaGF2ZSBzb21lIHN1Y2Nlc3NmdWwgcnVucyBvZiBjb21wb3MgaSBtaWdodCBjb2RlIGEgY29tcG8gc2VjdGlvbiBvZiB0aGUgc2l0ZS4=',154,NULL,1),(583,'Spot',1261375343,'KlNpdGVsb2dvIGVkaXRvciBmb3IgYWRtaW5zIGFkZGVkLiBPbmx5IGxvZ29zIHN1Ym1pdHRlZCBhZnRlciB0aGlzIGNoYW5nZSBoYXMgZWRpdGFibGUgY29udGVudC4=',145,NULL,1),(564,'Spot',1261271231,'SGV5ISBBcyBJIGhhdmUgYWRkZWQgcHJvcGVyIHN1cHBvcnQgZm9yIEFTQ0lJIGluIHRoZSBmb3J1bSBub3csIGxldCdzIGhhdmUgc29tZSBBU0NJSSBmdW4hIFBvc3QgeW91ciBsYXRlc3QgbG9nb3MgaW4gdGhpcyB0aHJlYWQh',147,NULL,1),(565,'Spot',1261271474,'',147,NULL,1),(566,'Spot',1261271525,'',147,NULL,1),(567,'Spot',1261271559,'',147,NULL,1),(568,'Spot',1261271600,'',147,'Last edited by Spot 2009-12-21 03:56',1),(569,'Spot',1261271669,'',147,NULL,1),(570,'Spot',1261271701,'',147,NULL,1),(571,'Spot',1261271847,'SGV5Li4uIGFsbCBhc2NpaWFyZW5hIHVzZXJzLCBsZXQncyBtYWtlIGEgbWVnYSBjby1vcCBjb2xseSENClBvc3QgeW91ciBsb2dvcyBpbiB0aGlzIHRocmVhZCwgYW5kIHdlIHB1dCBp